{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Records one realized conversational turn into the message store under a labeled venue (chat | agent-app | ...). This is the boundary a venue calls after the assistant reply is final — not an ambient hook in chat_llm, which every arm also drives; capturing there would flood the conversation stream with background traffic. Opt-in by venue keeps \"chat\" meaning what a human saw and said. Content-addressed and occurrence-idempotent (a replayed turn records once). Tool exchanges fold to one-line glue (name + args only, never the result payload) — narrative continuity without duplicating the session store, which keeps full fidelity.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse crate::agent::msg::put::put;","params":[{"desc":"The conversation label this turn belongs to (chat | agent-app | ...). Consumers filter by it; it is what lets 'chat' mean what a human saw, distinct from the raw llm firehose.","name":"venue","type":"String"},{"desc":"The venue's own message array for the realized turn: role/content rows, assistant tool_calls, tool results. System rows are skipped, tool exchanges fold to glue.","name":"messages","type":"JSONArray"},{"desc":"Who, when known - the session's username for a chat turn, empty otherwise. Empty string, never omitted.","name":"entity","type":"String"},{"desc":"The capturing venue/surface (agent-app, notebook, importer). A tag, never a branch.","name":"provenance","type":"String"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"tvoqtn1a0f70d35bes95f","readers":[],"time":1790851337402,"username":"system","writers":[]}